Subject: [PATCH 2/2] bluray: a seek leaves the end of the playlist

A BD-J program learns that its playlist has ended once per playlist:
the end is flagged when the reader reaches it, and reported to the
program only while the flag is fresh. Only opening a playlist cleared
it. A program that loops its playlist by seeking back to the start and
playing on - or a viewer seeking back once the end was read - got the
playlist's end reported the first time only; the second time it never
heard of it and sat on the last picture.

A seek now clears the flag, so the end is reported each time playback
reaches it.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 src/libbluray/bluray.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/libbluray/bluray.c b/src/libbluray/bluray.c
index d20f9f5..d331004 100644
--- a/src/libbluray/bluray.c
+++ b/src/libbluray/bluray.c
@@ -1754,6 +1754,7 @@ static int64_t _seek_internal(BLURAY *bd,
 
         /* update title position */
         bd->s_pos = (uint64_t)title_pkt * 192;
+        bd->end_of_playlist = 0;
 
         /* Update PSR_TIME */
         media_time = _update_time_psr_from_stream(bd);
